  "settings.agentApiKeys": { area: "layout", what: "SettingsSubPanels · API keys: a provider key saved to / removed from the OS keyring (input cleared, never read back), 'keyring locked' + Unlock (on a server: 'locked — sign in on a paired device', no Unlock), the per-CLI 'runs on' dropdown (own login / my API key, only once a key is saved / the administrator's key, only where offered — one at a time), the limit in million billed tokens with the ≈ $ estimate and an older build's dollar limit named as a hint, the agent-logins row's 'uses API key'; survives a restart" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.claude": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · Claude: a new local Claude tab runs on the key through the API proxy (no custom-key dialog; /status shows the proxy base URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN), runs without Remote Control; neither key nor token on any argv (ps), the key in no agent environment (/proc/<pid>/environ) or tmux launcher; removing the key stops the tab at its next turn; switched off → a new tab is back on the subscription login" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.workspace": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · Anthropic key not scoped to a workspace: Save lists the key's workspaces — with one it is saved at once, with several a picker appears (Save / Cancel), with none listable a wrkspc_ field; a workspace the key cannot use is refused and the picker stays; the saved row reads 'workspace wrkspc_…'; a Claude tab on the key then answers (no 'anthropic-workspace-id' error); a key saved before this fix shows the proxy's 'save it again to pick one' message" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.limit": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · monthly limit: Save needs a limit (20 proposed); the row shows '$x of $y spent this month', Set limit raises/lowers it; a turn's cost lands in the row within seconds of its end (and in <state_dir>/agent-api-usage.json within ~5 s, and at quit); at the limit a new Claude turn shows the budget message (no retries) and Gemini a RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED one, while a turn already running finishes; a key saved without a limit reads 'no monthly limit' and is refused until one is set; 'API budget reached' in the shared-logins row; a model not in the price table is listed under its provider; a turn cancelled mid-answer is still charged (by time, up to its max_tokens); a new UTC month starts from zero" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.gemini": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · Gemini: a new local Gemini tab gets a proxy token as GEMINI_API_KEY and GOOGLE_GEMINI_BASE_URL, and runs through the API proxy once 'Use Gemini API key' is picked in /auth (streaming answers arrive as they are written)" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.codex": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · OpenAI/Codex: save an OpenAI key with a monthly token limit, select my API key in Codex runs on, then open a new local Codex tab or resume a conversation; it uses a per-tab proxy token with HTTP Responses streaming, never the real key or saved ChatGPT login; usage includes cached input and reasoning output, compaction is metered, budget and key removal stop requests; switching back restores its own login on new tabs; not verified live" },
  "settings.agentApiKeys.opencode": { area: "layout", what: "API keys · OpenCode (1.x and 2): with an Anthropic, Gemini or OpenAI key saved, select my API key in OpenCode runs on (or + → OpenCode (API)), open a new local OpenCode tab and pick a model of a keyed provider in /models; its requests go through the proxy with a per-tab token (OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT names only {env:…}), even with a key or Claude login stored by opencode auth login; the row counts the turn, budget and key removal stop it; the Ollama models still list; a provider set in the user's own inline config keeps it; OpenCode 2's OpenAI WebSocket attempt falls back to HTTP; not verified live" },
